Requirements: 28   with obligations: 27   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Before any test is looked at, the review records — for each criterion it
    derived from the mandate — the concrete ways the delivered code could plausibly fail
    that criterion.
    -> pre-test-failure-modes  [functional/explicit]
       Before any test is looked at, record for each criterion derived from the mandate
       the concrete ways the delivered code could plausibly fail that criterion.

[constraint-01] Each recorded way of failing carries an identifier unique within the
    review, the criterion it belongs to, a classification, a free-text description, and
    the regions of changed source it implicates.
    -> recorded-failure-fields  [functional/explicit]
       Each recorded way of failing carries a unique identifier within the review, the
       criterion it belongs to, a classification, a free-text description, and the
       regions of changed source it implicates.

[constraint-02] Every other part of the review that names a recorded way of failing
    names it by that identifier, and does not restate its content.
    -> use-recorded-way-identifiers  [invariant/explicit]
       Every part of the review that refers to a recorded way of failing names it by its
       identifier rather than restating its content.

[constraint-03] A classification is either a value from a fixed vocabulary or a single
    escape value meaning the vocabulary has no value for this way of failing.
    -> classification-escape-value  [invariant/explicit]
       A classification is either a value from the fixed vocabulary or a single escape
       value meaning the vocabulary has no value for this way of failing.

[constraint-04] The recorded ways of failing persist with the rest of the review's
    state, and a review reloaded from storage carries them unchanged.
    -> persist-recorded-failures  [invariant/explicit]
       The recorded ways of failing persist with the rest of the review's state, and a
       review reloaded from storage carries them unchanged.

[constraint-05] The step that produces them is given the criterion and the changed
    source, and is given no test.
    -> no-test-for-recording-step  [functional/explicit]
       The step that produces recorded ways of failing is given the criterion and the
       changed source, and is not given a test.

[constraint-06] That step is guided by a checklist of ways to fail chosen by the
    criterion's type, and may still record a way of failing that no entry on that
    checklist names.
    -> checklist-guided-failure-recording  [functional/explicit]
       The step that records ways of failing is guided by a checklist of ways to fail
       chosen by the criterion's type, while still allowing it to record a way of
       failing that no checklist entry names.

[constraint-07] Recording no way of failing for a criterion is a valid result for that
    criterion, and carries the reason the set is empty.
    -> empty-failing-set-valid-with-reason  [invariant/explicit]
       Recording no way of failing for a criterion is a valid result for that criterion,
       and the review carries the reason the set is empty.

[constraint-08] A criterion's set of records is reused rather than produced again
    exactly while both that criterion's text and the contents of the source regions its
    records implicate are unchanged.
    -> reuse-recorded-set-when-criterion-and-source-unchanged  [regression/explicit]
       A criterion's set of records is reused rather than produced again exactly while
       both that criterion's text and the contents of the source regions its records
       implicate are unchanged.

[constraint-09] A criterion whose text changed has its entire set produced again, and
    keeps no part of the set recorded for it before.
    -> recompute-changed-criterion-records  [invariant/explicit]
       A criterion whose text changed has its entire set of recorded ways of failing
       produced again, with no part of the previously recorded set retained for that
       criterion.

[constraint-10] A run continuing an earlier run reuses every set it is entitled to
    reuse, and produces again only the sets it is not.
    -> reuse-entitled-sets-on-continued-run  [functional/explicit]
       A continuing run reuses every set it is entitled to reuse.

[constraint-11] Where a set was reused rather than produced again, the review says so.
    -> reuse-says-so  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Where a set was reused rather than produced again, the review says so.

[constraint-12] The review reports the recorded ways of failing.
    -> report-recorded-ways-of-failing  [functional/explicit]
       The review reports the recorded ways of failing.

[constraint-13] Whether the review reports the work complete, and every rating it gives
    a criterion, are what they would be if no way of failing had been recorded at all.
    -> completion-and-ratings-unchanged  [invariant/explicit]
       The review reports completion and every criterion rating exactly as it would if
       no way of failing had been recorded.

[exclusion-01] Judging whether any test would fail if the delivered code contained a
    recorded way of failing.
    -> no-test-judgment-about-recorded-failure  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not add judging whether any test would fail if the delivered code
       contained a recorded way of failing.

[exclusion-02] Deriving any rating, classification or conclusion about a criterion from
    its recorded ways of failing.
    -> no-derive-ratings-from-recorded-failures  [invariant/explicit]
       The change does not derive any rating, classification, or conclusion about a
       criterion from its recorded ways of failing.

[exclusion-03] Which criteria the review derives from the mandate, and how it derives
    them.
    -> derive-criteria-from-mandate-and-method  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not alter which criteria the review derives from the mandate or
       how it derives them.

[exclusion-04] How the review gathers, judges or rates test evidence today.
    -> no-test-evidence-gathering-judgment-rating  [docs_config/explicit]
       The change does not alter how the review gathers, judges, or rates test evidence
       today.

[exclusion-05] Running the delivered code, and altering it to produce a failure.
    -> no-runtime-failure-injection  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not include running the delivered code or altering it to produce
       a failure.

[exclusion-06] Comparing a recorded set against an expected set supplied from outside
    the review.
    -> no-external-expected-set-comparison  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not compare a recorded set against an expected set supplied from
       outside the review.

[completion-01] Implementation.
    -- no obligation, deliberately
       The requirement is only the section marker "Implementation." standing alone, with
       no substantive requirement under it.

[completion-02] A test fails when the step that records ways of failing is given a test.
    -> test-fails-when-step-given-test  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that the step that records ways of failing is given a test.

[completion-03] A test fails when a criterion with no plausible way of failing is given
    an invented one instead of an empty set carrying its reason.
    -> test-empty-set-with-reason  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a criterion with no plausible way of failing is given an
       empty set carrying its reason instead of an invented way of failing.

[completion-04] A test fails when a set is produced again across two continued runs
    although the criterion's text and the contents of its implicated source regions are
    both unchanged.
    -> reuse-unchanged-set-across-continued-runs  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a set is reused rather than produced again across two
       continued runs when the criterion's text and the contents of its implicated
       source regions are both unchanged.

[completion-05] A test fails when a criterion whose text changed keeps any part of the
    set recorded for it before.
    -> changed-criterion-keeps-no-prior-records  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a criterion whose text changed keeps no part of the set
       recorded for it before.

[completion-06] A test fails when a criterion whose text is unchanged has its set
    produced again because a different criterion's text changed.
    -> test-fails-unchanged-criterion-reused-after-other-change  [test_demand/explicit]
       A test asserts that a criterion whose text is unchanged has its set produced
       again because a different criterion's text changed.

[completion-07] A test fails when recording ways of failing changes the review's
    completion conclusion or any criterion's rating.
    -> completion-07-no-rating-or-conclusion-change  [regression/explicit]
       Recording ways of failing does not change the review's completion conclusion or
       any criterion's rating.

[completion-08] Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review
    state and byte-identical report output.
    -> byte-identical-runs  [regression/explicit]
       Two recorded runs over the same input produce byte-identical review state and
       byte-identical report output.
